    Reach the last line with a test double
    
    yarn cover shows one line our tests never run: the default in
    gradePoints(). It throws when a letter grade has no grade points.
    
    No input can get there. gradePoints() only ever sees what
    getLetterGrade() returns, and getLetterGrade() only returns A to F.
    Every case the spec describes is already tested; this line is for a
    case the spec can't produce.
    
    We can still reach it, with the move from last lecture. computeGPA
    depends on a LetterGrader interface instead of grading directly, the
    real grader moves into PercentLetterGrader, and a test passes in a
    MadeUpLetterGrader that returns "G". Coverage is now 100%.
    
    Look at what that cost: an interface, a new class, a constructor
    parameter, and a double, all so one test can check something that
    can't happen. And the test checks behaviour the spec never promised:
    computeGPA's docs don't say it throws. Is that worth it?

